      "hints": [
        "General term: $\\binom{5}{r}(2x)^{5-r}\\left(-\\frac{1}{x}\\right)^r = \\binom{5}{r}2^{5-r}(-1)^r x^{5-2r}$.",
        "Set $5 - 2r = 1 \\implies r = 2$.",
        "Evaluate $\\binom{5}{2} 2^3 (-1)^2 = 80$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Write the general term $T_{r+1}$ in the binomial expansion of $\\left(2x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^5$:\n$$T_{r+1} = \\binom{5}{r}(2x)^{5-r}\\left(-\\frac{1}{x}\\right)^r = \\binom{5}{r}2^{5-r}(-1)^r x^{5-2r}$$",
        "To find the term in $x = x^1$, set the exponent of $x$ equal to $1$:\n$$5 - 2r = 1 \\implies 2r = 4 \\implies r = 2$$",
        "Evaluate the coefficient for $r = 2$:\n$$\\text{Coefficient of } x = \\binom{5}{2}2^{5-2}(-1)^2 = 10 \\times 8 \\times 1 = 80$$"
      ],
